= Staal's Health Deteriorates

Unbeknownst to the public, Staal has been suffering from pernicious anemia for several years. As early as 4295, his family doctor warned him that, given the stress and heavy responsibilities of his career, he likely had no more than six years to live. Now, with the added strain of the chancellorship, those who interact with him have begun to notice his steady decline into lethargy. He may only have a few months left.

In a public announcement, Staal announces his resignation, stating that he will soon handpick a successor to be appointed by DuFour. He never truly enjoyed the role, and in recent months has quietly delegated his duties to trusted allies in the Commonwealth Army, grooming them to take his place.

The question now: who will carry forward Staal's legacy?

- @schleicher_dead

